      "source_id": "corpus:12be10a9caef19ae0064a8ce4f0c0ae6240963a0810c52823f24fa319b10c743:file:2391",
      "target": ") and ash (the spent residue). FFUSE: the seer interprets the smoke's shape, direction, thickness, and color, reconstituting the scattered visual signals into a prophetic message. VINIT: the unlit kindling and unburned incense. TANCH: the brazier or censer as container. AFWD: smoke rising straight and strong (auspicious). AREV: smoke descending or blowing back toward the seer (warning, blockage). ENGAGR: smoke that forms a shape recognizable as two contradictory omens simultaneously.\"\n}"
